# @hsk-sync:notes-browse

Token `@hsk-sync:notes-browse` marks the folder **Sort and view** control and listing rules shared by VS Code **Notes Icons Browse** and Harrix Notes Android.

The Android notes browser lives in `D:\GitHub\harrix-notes-android` (not `android/` in this repo — that is the HSK utility app).

If the toolbar button, menu items, or listing behavior change on either side, update the other.

## Sibling implementations

| Side | Path |
|------|------|
| VS Code | `vscode/harrix-notes-explorer-hsk/icons-browse*.js`, `media/icons-browse.*` |
| Android | `D:\GitHub\harrix-notes-android` — `NotesBrowseLayout`, `NotesSortBy`, `NotesListingOptions`, `NotesFolderSortViewMenuContent` |

## Contract

Toolbar: Material **Sort** icon (`M3 18h6v-2H3v2zM3 6v2h18V6H3zm0 7h12v-2H3v2z`). Click opens a dropdown (does not toggle layout).

Menu (same labels and order):

1. List / Table / Icons / Thumbnails / Tree — radio, leading ViewList / TableRows / GridView / Dashboard / AccountTree, trailing check
2. separator
3. Name / Date / Size — radio, leading check
4. separator
5. Folders on top / Reverse order / Show .g.md files / Show dates — checkboxes

Listing (`NotesListingOptions.apply`): hide `*.g.md` notes unless Show .g.md; sort by display name / mtime / size; optional reverse; optional folders first. Show a folder only if it (or a descendant) contains a Markdown note. Show dates only in **list** rows (`dd.MM.yyyy` for filename/YAML, `dd.MM.yyyy, HH:mm` for file times). **Table** always shows Name / Date / Type / Size; header click on Name, Date, or Size sets that sort (same column toggles reverse; a new column starts ascending). Type is not sortable. Folder size is blank unless `sizeBytes > 0`. Type is Folder or Note (`.g.md` is still a note). **Thumbnails** cards show featured image / canvas / first Markdown or `img/` image, else a text excerpt; dates stay list-only. **Tree** shows listable folders from the notes root with expand/collapse (default collapsed; the path to the current folder stays open). Expand all / Collapse all sit above the tree; Collapse all keeps the current-folder path open. One icon grid sits under the current folder.

## Change checklist

- Keep option names, icons, and sort/filter semantics identical.
- After VS Code changes: `hsk vscode format` / `hsk vscode check` / `hsk vscode sync-notes-explorer`.
- After Android changes: `hsk android format` / `hsk android check` in `harrix-notes-android`.
